§§ `s 65(6)(a) -- the permission as a regulative rule (read with #TRACE; a DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT)`

-- Window opens 1 April 2025, the period begins 1 October 2025: the window is 183 days long (days 0 to 182; 30 September is day 182).
-- Expected: a claim on day 0 (FULFILLED), on day 182 (the last day: FULFILLED) and on day 183 (too late: the permission has lapsed, FULFILLED because a lapsed MAY is benign).
#TRACE `s 65(6)(a) the person may claim in advance` (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 1 10 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 65(6)(a) the person to whom the claim relates` DOES `s 65(6)(a) makes the claim for an attendance allowance` AT 0
#TRACE `s 65(6)(a) the person may claim in advance` (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 1 10 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 65(6)(a) the person to whom the claim relates` DOES `s 65(6)(a) makes the claim for an attendance allowance` AT 182
#TRACE `s 65(6)(a) the person may claim in advance` (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 1 10 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 65(6)(a) the person to whom the claim relates` DOES `s 65(6)(a) makes the claim for an attendance allowance` AT 183
